═══ R8 EN reply complete (collagen/vegetarian) — guard: passed_after_retry ═══
Q: I have spondylosis and osteoporosis and my doctor requires me to take collagen as part of treatment. But I have been a vegetarian for 14 years. Can I take normal collagen?
Sources: Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) | Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: qa_metaphysics,qa_general,introduction
  ✓ substantial reply (>600 chars)
  ✓ ends cleanly (punctuation/emoji, not mid-word)
  ✓ answers the vegetarian-collagen question
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Thank you for asking before taking it — after 14 years, you clearly take your vow seriously 🙏

Master Lu addressed this exact type of situation. In *Answered — Frequently Asked Questions About Practising Buddhism* (Q115), he said:

> When you consume any medicine or health supplements that contain ingredients such as gelatine or fish oil, if your body does not reject the taste, then perhaps you have not reached the level where you are completely observing your precepts. However, it would still be best to avoid consuming such products as they contain animal by-products.

So the principle is: **avoid it if you can find another way** — but this is not the same as deliberately eating meat for enjoyment. Master Lu taught that what matters most is your intention. If you are taking something purely because you have no choice medically, and there is no craving or enjoyment in your heart, you should tell Guan Yin Bodhisattva in your mind that you are doing this out of necessity and that you do not want it at all. Master Lu taught that breaking a precept happens when you find yourself *enjoying* it — in that case one would recite the Eighty-Eight Buddhas Great Repentance 49 times and sincerely repent, then make the vow again.

**Practical suggestions first, before you compromise the vow:**

- Ask your doctor whether **plant-based / vegan collagen** or collagen-boosting supplements (vitamin C, silica, plant protein) can serve the same purpose. Many are available now.
- Master Lu recommended vegetarians take **soy products** (soybeans, tofu, tofu sheets, soy milk) as they are high in protein, and **milk and dairy products** to replenish calcium and other essential nutrients — this is directly relevant for osteoporosis.
- He also mentioned **calcium and soy lecithin supplements** as acceptable health supplements for vegetarians.

Heart Dharma Door teaches caring for both body and spirit — Master Lu never asked anyone to refuse medical treatment. Please keep following your doctor. If after exploring alternatives there is genuinely no option, take it as medicine, not as food, and speak to Guan Yin Bodhisattva in your heart.

May I ask — are you already doing daily chanting? If yes, I can suggest what Master Lu taught for bone and spine conditions. If not, I can show you a simple way to begin 🙏

If you'd like face-to-face guidance, the Heart Dharma Door centres are free to visit:
🌐 https://xlfm.my/contact-us
📞 +603-6257 3811

*Reference: Answered — Frequently Asked Questions About Practising Buddhism (Q115, Q150)*

